From a3f2229a5fcd47434ad3dc2a653bc89932ed0bb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:19:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Phone briefing: two tiles per row on every front, as on Tech

News, Sports and Entertainment squeezed every tile into one row on phones,
so values like "Brazilian Grand Prix" and "Election" broke mid-word. The
phone briefing now uses Tech's two-per-row grid on every front; an odd last
tile spans the row. Word values break between words and ease from 26px to
20px on narrow phones. Desktop and tablet are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BeSUhTLXvQhUDsTovwqjsi
